---
export const prerender = true;

import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions — Unknown Sender"
  description="Terms and conditions for using the Unknown Sender website and taking part in the experience."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <article class="page">
    <div class="wrap-narrow">
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
      <div class="updated">Last updated: August 2026</div>

      <section>
        <p>These terms govern your use of the Unknown Sender website, the Unknown Sender mobile
          app, and your participation in any Unknown Sender experience. By using this website,
          the app, or booking a ticket, you agree to these terms.</p>
        <p>Unknown Sender is operated by <strong>Treadwell21</strong>, a company registered in
          England and Wales, company number <strong>16996311</strong>, with registered address at
          71&ndash;75 Shelton Street, Covent Garden, London, WC2H 9JQ, United Kingdom.
          Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@unknownsender.co.uk">hello@unknownsender.co.uk</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>About the experience</h2>
        <p>Unknown Sender is a real-world, story-led mystery played on foot through a UK city.
          Players receive messages, images and other content through the Unknown Sender app on
          their phone, and follow clues through real streets and venues. Sessions last
          approximately 90&ndash;120 minutes.</p>
        <p>Participation requires:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A smartphone (iOS or Android) capable of installing the Unknown Sender app,
            available on the {/* TODO: swap "#" for real store URLs once live */}
            <a href="#" rel="noopener">App Store</a> and
            <a href="#" rel="noopener">Google Play</a>.</li>
          <li>An active mobile data connection for the duration of the session.</li>
          <li>Sufficient battery to complete the session (we recommend at least 80% at start,
            and bringing a portable battery).</li>
          <li>The ability to walk and stand for the full session.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Players are responsible for their own safety, including observing traffic rules and
          the law at all times. See our <a href="/before-you-play">Before you play</a> brief.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Eligibility</h2>
        <p>Players must be 18 years of age or over. By booking, you confirm that you and every
          member of your team meet this age requirement.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Tickets and bookings</h2>
        <p>Tickets are sold through this website in pounds sterling (GBP), processed by Stripe.
          A booking is confirmed once payment has been received and a confirmation email issued.
          Each ticket is valid for 90 days from purchase and can be redeemed once.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Refunds and cancellations</h2>
        <p>See our <a href="/refunds">Refund Policy</a>. Briefly: full refund within 14 days of
          purchase if you haven&rsquo;t started; transfers to another player allowed any time within
          the 90-day validity window; once started, tickets are non-refundable.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Conduct during the experience</h2>
        <p>Players must behave lawfully and respectfully towards other players, members of the
          public, and staff at any venues featured in the experience. We reserve the right to
          terminate a session, without refund, if a player behaves in a way that is unsafe,
          abusive, or that puts the experience or other people at risk.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Personal property</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for your own belongings during the experience. Unknown Sender is
          not responsible for any theft, loss or damage to personal property. See
          <a href="/before-you-play">Before you play</a> for practical guidance.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Leaderboards</h2>
        <p>By completing a session you agree that your team name and score may be displayed on
          the public leaderboard for that game. No personal information beyond team name is
          published. You can request removal from the leaderboard at any time by email.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>All content on this website and within the experience, text, images, narrative,
          software, is the property of Treadwell21 unless otherwise stated. You may not copy,
          reproduce or commercially exploit any part of it without our written permission.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Liability</h2>
        <p>The experience takes place in real public spaces. We are not responsible for the
          actions of third parties or for events outside our reasonable control. Nothing in these
          terms limits or excludes our liability for death or personal injury caused by our
          negligence, for fraud, or for any other liability that cannot lawfully be limited or
          excluded.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>If something has gone wrong, please tell us so we can put it right. Email
          <a href="mailto:hello@unknownsender.co.uk">hello@unknownsender.co.uk</a> with a
          short description of what happened and your booking code where applicable. We aim to
          acknowledge complaints within two working days and to resolve them within ten working
          days.</p>
        <p>If we&rsquo;re unable to resolve your complaint to your satisfaction, you may have the
          right to refer it to an Alternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) provider, or to take it
          to the county court. Nothing in this process affects your statutory rights under UK
          consumer law.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and any disputes will be
          subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The date at the top of the page indicates
          when they were last changed.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding: 80px 0; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); margin: 12px 0 12px; }
  .updated { color: var(--ink-dim); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 40px; }
  section { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--ink-dim); text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 16px; padding-bottom: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  p { margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.65; }
  a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
